#### [P0-2] Add Confidence Level Markers (VERIFIED/LIKELY/UNCERTAIN/BROKEN/UNKNOWN)

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: None
**Spec Reference**: CLAUDE.md lines 148-149, 561 (Conservative completion, Status taxonomy) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-09-043855.md section 3 (Confidence Calibration, lines 279-316)

##### Description

Current evaluations report ✅ or ❌ without indicating confidence level. Users cannot distinguish between "I ran this and it works" vs "tests pass so probably works" vs "code looks reasonable" vs "can't verify, user should check". This ambiguity leads to wasted time on validation attempts and unclear risk assessment.

**New Requirement**: All assessments must use explicit confidence markers. Executive Summary must report confidence distribution and recommend user testing session if UNCERTAIN + UNKNOWN > 40%.

##### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Both evaluator agents include "Assessment Confidence Levels" section defining 5 markers
- [ ] Markers defined: ✅ VERIFIED (ran it, works), ✅ LIKELY (tests pass, code reasonable), ⚠️ UNCERTAIN (can't verify), ❌ BROKEN (ran it, fails), ❓ UNKNOWN (not evaluated)
- [ ] STATUS template includes confidence distribution in Executive Summary (VERIFIED: X%, LIKELY: Y%, etc.)
- [ ] Workflow rule documented: "If UNCERTAIN + UNKNOWN > 40% → recommend user manual testing session"
- [ ] Examples provided for each confidence level with specific evidence types
- [ ] Tested with sample evaluation showing mixed confidence levels across features
- [ ] Tested that confidence distribution appears in Executive Summary with recommendation when >40% uncertain/unknown

##### Technical Notes

**Files to modify**:
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/project-evaluator.md` (lines 110-118)
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/work-evaluator.md` (lines 107-116)

**Integration point**: Confidence levels work with evidence tables from P0-1. Evidence type determines confidence level:
- Screenshot/log showing success → VERIFIED
- Tests pass, no runtime → LIKELY
- Missing config/blocked → UNCERTAIN
- Error in logs → BROKEN
- Not checked this iteration → UNKNOWN

