#### [P0-3] Require Test Quality Verification with Evidence

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: None
**Spec Reference**: CLAUDE.md lines 396-402 (Never use MagicMock, Tests must fail with stubs) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-09-043855.md section 4 (Validation Enforcement, lines 420-460)

##### Description

Both evaluators say "test the tests" but don't enforce it. Current guidance is ADVICE ("Quick test: Break something obvious"), not REQUIREMENT. LLMs can skip this step and trust worthless tests that always pass regardless of implementation correctness.

**New Requirement**: For any project with tests, evaluator MUST verify tests actually catch bugs by introducing obvious bugs and documenting whether tests fail. If this step is skipped, test quality must be marked "UNKNOWN - not verified".

##### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Both evaluators include "Test Quality Verification (REQUIRED)" section
- [ ] Process documented: 1) Identify critical function, 2) Introduce obvious bug, 3) Run test suite, 4) Document result
- [ ] Evidence table template provided: Function Modified | Bug Introduced | Tests Run | Result | Verdict
- [ ] Examples provided showing tests that catch bugs (✅) vs tests that miss bugs (❌)
- [ ] STATUS template includes "Test Quality" section with: Verified modules, Blind spots, Recommendations
- [ ] Rule documented: "If you skip this step: Mark test quality as 'UNKNOWN - not verified'"
- [ ] Tested with sample evaluation showing test quality verification results
- [ ] Tested that blind spots are reported when tests pass despite introduced bugs

##### Technical Notes

**Files to modify**:
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/project-evaluator.md` (line 70, expand to full section)
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/work-evaluator.md` (similar addition)

**Critical insight**: This directly prevents trusting test suites that are "theater" - they run and pass but don't actually validate functionality. The evidence table forces documentation of what was tested and whether tests are real.

