#### [P1-1] Add User-Specified Workflow Gate Strictness

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: P0-2 (Confidence Levels)
**Spec Reference**: User requirement #1 (User-specified gates) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-09-043855.md section 4 (Validation Enforcement, lines 461-503)

##### Description

Current STATUS report has no enforcement mechanism preventing implementers from proceeding when validation is incomplete. User requirement: **Workflow gates should be user-specified**, either:
- Inline in slash command (e.g., `/do:it --strict` vs `/do:it --advisory`)
- Or user is prompted to pick strictness if not specified

Gates check: Critical issues resolved, validation confidence threshold, manual debt bounded, no active PAUSE.

##### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Both evaluator agents include "Workflow Gates" section defining 4 gates
- [ ] Gates defined: 1) Critical Issues Resolved (no P0/P1 bugs, no BROKEN features), 2) Validation Confidence Threshold (VERIFIED+LIKELY >= 60%, UNCERTAIN+UNKNOWN < 30%), 3) Manual Debt Bounded (<=5 items, no HIGH >3 days), 4) No Active PAUSE
- [ ] Gate strictness levels defined: BLOCKING (must pass to proceed), ADVISORY (warn but allow), DISABLED (no gates)
- [ ] Commands (/do:it, /do:it) accept `--gates=blocking|advisory|disabled` parameter
- [ ] If `--gates` not specified, command prompts user: "Choose workflow gate strictness: [blocking/advisory/disabled]"
- [ ] Implementer agents (test-driven-implementer, iterative-implementer) check gates before starting work
- [ ] BLOCKING mode: If gates fail, implementers output STOP message with details and refuse to proceed
- [ ] ADVISORY mode: If gates fail, implementers output warning but continue
- [ ] DISABLED mode: Gates not checked
- [ ] Example STOP message template provided showing which gates failed and why
- [ ] Tested with BLOCKING mode: Implementer stops when confidence <60%
- [ ] Tested with ADVISORY mode: Implementer warns but continues
- [ ] Tested with DISABLED mode: No gate checks performed
- [ ] Tested user prompt appears when --gates not specified

##### Technical Notes

**Files to modify**:
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/project-evaluator.md` (add Workflow Gates section after Critical Rules)
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/work-evaluator.md` (add Workflow Gates section)
