#### [P1-2] Create VALIDATION_DEBT.md Ledger File

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: P0-4 (Deterministic Validation Check)
**Spec Reference**: User requirement #2 (Validation debt tracking) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-09-043855.md section 3 (Confidence Calibration, lines 351-378)

##### Description

User requirement: **Use VALIDATION_DEBT.md ledger file** to track items never validated across sessions. Currently, if 5 evaluations each defer 2-3 manual items, user has 10-15 unvalidated items with no consolidated list. Prevents items from being forgotten.

Evaluators update ledger after each evaluation. When debt >5 items OR 2+ HIGH priority, recommend user "validation session" to clear debt.

##### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Ledger template created: `.agent_planning/VALIDATION_DEBT.md`
- [ ] Template includes table: Item | Why Not Automated | Suggested User Steps | Added | Priority | Status
- [ ] Template includes Debt Score summary: N items (X HIGH, Y MED, Z LOW)
- [ ] Both evaluators documented to update ledger after each evaluation
- [ ] Process documented: 1) Read existing ledger, 2) Add new USER_VALIDATES items, 3) Check for user sign-offs (Status changed from "Pending" to "Validated: YYYY-MM-DD"), 4) Carry forward unvalidated items
- [ ] Recommendation rule: "When debt >5 items OR 2+ HIGH: Recommend user validation session"
- [ ] Implementer agents check ledger for unvalidated HIGH priority items before proceeding
- [ ] BLOCKING gate mode prevents proceeding when >5 items or 2+ HIGH unvalidated (integrates with P1-1)
- [ ] Tested: Evaluator adds new manual item to ledger
- [ ] Tested: User marks item "Validated: 2025-12-09" in ledger, next evaluation recognizes sign-off
- [ ] Tested: Debt accumulates across multiple evaluations
- [ ] Tested: Recommendation appears when thresholds exceeded

##### Technical Notes

**Files to create**:
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/.agent_planning/VALIDATION_DEBT.md` (template)

**Files to modify**:
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/project-evaluator.md` (add ledger update step)
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/work-evaluator.md` (add ledger update step)
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/test-driven-implementer.md` (add ledger check)
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/iterative-implementer.md` (add ledger check)

**Ledger workflow**:
1. Evaluator determines item requires USER_VALIDATES (per P0-4 policy)
2. Evaluator adds row to ledger with Priority (based on impact), Suggested Steps (specific instructions)
3. User executes validation steps, edits ledger to change Status from "Pending" to "Validated: YYYY-MM-DD"
4. Next evaluation reads ledger, sees sign-off, proceeds with confidence
5. If user doesn't validate, item persists in ledger and counts toward debt threshold

**Integration**: This ledger is the mechanism that enforces user confirmation requirement from P0-4. Each evaluation checks ledger for pending HIGH priority items and includes debt score in gate calculations.

