#### [P1-3] Elevate "Runtime Trumps Tests" to Top-Level Principle

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Small (1-2 days)
**Dependencies**: P0-1 (Runtime Verification)
**Spec Reference**: CLAUDE.md lines 396-402 (Test Writing rules), 559-569 (Quality Standards) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-09-043855.md section 2 (Critical Risk #2, lines 174-211)

##### Description

Critical principle "Trust runtime over tests" currently buried as bullet point at line 275 in project-evaluator. This is easily ignored by LLMs despite being fundamental. Tests are easier to verify than runtime (just run pytest), so LLMs take path of least resistance and trust passing tests even when runtime fails.

**New Requirement**: Elevate to top-level H2 section "Critical Principle: Runtime Trumps Tests" appearing BEFORE main evaluation sections. Require explicit runtime vs test reconciliation in STATUS output.

##### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Both evaluators include new H2 section "Critical Principle: Runtime Trumps Tests" near top of prompt (before evaluation sections)
- [ ] Section states: "ALWAYS ALWAYS ALWAYS: If runtime fails, tests mean nothing"
- [ ] Verification process documented: 1) Run tests → document pass/fail, 2) Run software → document works/broken, 3) Reconcile
- [ ] Reconciliation rule: "If tests pass BUT runtime fails → tests are WORTHLESS (report this explicitly)"
- [ ] STATUS template includes "Runtime vs Tests Reconciliation" section
- [ ] Reconciliation section shows: Tests (X/Y passing), Runtime (flows tested with results), Verdict (blind spots when tests pass but runtime fails)
- [ ] Example provided showing tests passing but feature broken, explicitly calling out test blind spot
- [ ] Tested with scenario where tests pass but runtime fails - evaluator reports "Tests have BLIND SPOT" in Reconciliation section
- [ ] Old buried bullet point (line 275) removed from Critical Rules section to avoid duplication

##### Technical Notes

**Files to modify**:
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/project-evaluator.md` (move line 275 → new H2 section before line 41, expand significantly)
- `/Users/bmf/icode/loom99-claude-marketplace/plugins/do-more-now/agents/work-evaluator.md` (add same H2 section)

**Position**: Place immediately after "Profile Loading" section (from Status recommendation) but before "Does It Actually Work?" section. This ensures principle is seen early and influences evaluation approach throughout.

**Integration with P0-1**: Runtime verification evidence tables (P0-1) provide the data for runtime vs tests reconciliation. If evidence shows runtime failure but tests pass, this principle mandates explicit reporting of test inadequacy.

